      "content": "I see. You're focusing on the \"variables\" introduced by the social aspect. Can you dig a bit deeper into why the communal/religious aspect specifically increases risk? Like, is there a correlation between those types of frequent, large-scale social gatherings and higher incidents of sudden lifestyle shifts or instability compared to someone more isolated?",
